.TH "COPY-SONG-URL.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
copy\-song\-url.sh \- copy the currently playing media URL to the clipboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBcopy\-song\-url.sh\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read xesam:url from go\-playerctl metadata, require an HTTP(S) URL, and copy it using wl\-copy, xclip or xsel (in that order). Print the URL on success.
.SH NOTES
Requires go\-playerctl and a supported clipboard program. Exits with an error if there is no shareable media URL.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires go-playerctl, a player publishing MPRIS metadata with the
xesam:url field, and a usable clipboard utility: wl-copy, xclip
or xsel. The first installed clipboard utility wins in that order;
ensure it matches the current Wayland or X11 session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
go-playerctl metadata xesam:url
copy-song-url.sh
.fi
.PP
The helper accepts only http:// and https:// URLs, writes the URL
to the clipboard, and prints it on stdout. Avoid logging stdout if
the URL contains a private access token.
.SH FAILURE MODES
Missing go-playerctl or a clipboard utility exits 127. Missing
media or a URL using another scheme exits 1. If copying appears
successful but pasting fails, inspect the graphical session and
the chosen clipboard utility.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires go-playerctl, a media player publishing xesam:url over
MPRIS, and a usable clipboard command: wl-copy, xclip or xsel.
The helper tries those clipboard programs in that order.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
go-playerctl metadata xesam:url
copy-song-url.sh
.fi
.SH FAILURE MODES
Missing go-playerctl or all clipboard utilities causes exit 127.
Missing or non-HTTP(S) URLs cause exit 1. The URL is printed to
stdout as well as copied to the clipboard; avoid recording it in
public logs if it contains private access data.
.SH SEE ALSO
go\-playerctl(1)
